{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And a man or a woman, etc.</b> It was necessary to specify here ״or a woman״ and not say ״a man״ with woman included, since a woman has no beard — one might say that the verse spoke only of a man who has a beard. And even though it says ״a man״ [adam] and does not say ״a man״ [ish], you might say it comes to include the minor or to exclude gentiles, and in any case nega'im of the beard do not render a woman impure — therefore Scripture says ״or a woman,״ for if hair grew in the place of her beard it does render impure through netakim."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:55:58.229462371Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}